# ⏳ AETHERIA — TIME SYSTEM

> **Time does not stop when the Master does.**
>
> The world of Aetheria continues to move.
>
> Characters live, NPCs act, factions move, events occur, and the world changes as time passes.

---

# 📌 1. OVERVIEW

The **Time System** is the global system responsible for controlling and tracking the passage of time within Aetheria.

Time is treated as a fundamental part of the world simulation.

The system controls:

```text
Second
Minute
Hour
Day
Night
Week
Month
Season
Year
```

Time is then used by other systems:

```text
Time System
     ↓
Game State System
     ↓
┌───────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┐
│               │               │
NPC State    World State     Event State
│               │               │
Quest State  Faction State   Character State
```

---

# 🎯 2. PURPOSE

The Time System exists to create a living world.

Without a Time System:

```text
NPC
↓
Always available
```

With a Time System:

```text
NPC
↓
Morning → Working
Afternoon → Working
Evening → Tavern
Night → Sleeping
```

The world therefore becomes dynamic rather than static.

---

# 🧠 3. CORE PRINCIPLE

The Time System follows one primary rule:

> **The world has its own clock.**

The Master does not directly control the passage of time.

Instead:

```text
WORLD TIME
    ↓
TIME SYSTEM
    ↓
GAME STATE SYSTEM
    ↓
WORLD CHANGES
```

The Master can influence events, but normal time continues to progress.

