# 🔄 30. GAME STATE SYSTEM UPDATE

The Time System provides time information.

The **Game State System** determines what that time means for the world.

Architecture:

```text
TIME SYSTEM
     │
     ▼
CURRENT TIME
     │
     ▼
GAME STATE SYSTEM
     │
 ┌───┼────┬────┬────┬────┐
 │   │    │    │    │    │
NPC World Quest Event Faction
 │   │    │    │    │
 └───┴────┴────┴────┴────┘
             │
             ▼
       STATE CHANGES
             │
             ▼
       DATABASE SYSTEM
```

---

# 🧠 31. IMPORTANT RULE

The Time System should **not directly control every game system**.

Instead:

```text
TIME SYSTEM
```

provides:

```text
"What time is it?"
```

while:

```text
GAME STATE SYSTEM
```

determines:

```text
"What happens because of that time?"
```

This keeps the architecture modular.

---

# 🧱 32. TIME SYSTEM MODULES

Recommended structure:

```text
TIME SYSTEM
│
├── TimeManager
├── Clock
├── Calendar
├── TimeScale
├── TimeOfDay
├── SeasonManager
├── TimeEventScheduler
├── TimeCondition
└── TimePersistence
```

### TimeManager

Main coordinator.

### Clock

Tracks hour, minute, and second.

### Calendar

Tracks day, month, and year.

### TimeScale

Controls game-time speed.

### TimeOfDay

Determines morning, afternoon, evening, and night.

### SeasonManager

Controls seasonal progression.

### TimeEventScheduler

Schedules time-based events.

### TimeCondition

Checks conditions such as:

```text
Before
After
Between
Exact Time
Exact Date
```

### TimePersistence

Stores world time in the Database System.

